v1.0.54: Eliminate parent setState on every wheel tick — picker is now truly lag-free

Root cause of remaining lag (v1.0.53): CupertinoDatePicker.onDateTimeChanged and
CupertinoPicker.onSelectedItemChanged fire CONTINUOUSLY while the user scrolls
the wheel. Each tick was calling parent's setState, which rebuilt the entire
modal ListView (all sections, all text fields, all image pickers) — thousands
of widgets per scroll tick.

Fix in lib/core/widgets/inline_picker_row.dart:
- Each wheel tick now updates an internal ValueListenable / mutable state
  in the picker's own State, not the parent's.
- The additionalInfo row rebuilds via ValueListenableBuilder + RepaintBoundary
  (scoped to that single text widget — no parent rebuild).
- Parent's setState only fires on "Selesai" tap (onConfirmed callback),
  exactly once per close.

Also: removed _onStartDateChanged / _onEndDateChanged from manual_booking_modal
(now handled via onConfirmed lambdas in the InlineDatePickerRow site).

Verified:
- flutter analyze: 0 issues
- flutter test: 89/89 passing
- Tanggal Mulai picker: value "8 Sep 2026" updates realtime as wheel scrolled,
  picker stayed open across rapid close/open stress (3x), Selesai commit works.
- All 3 modals (Kostum Baru / Cicilan Baru / Booking Manual) inline pickers
  verified visually.

